{
  "_what": "The instruction, command and skill files the person already keeps for their other AIs, read in place and labelled by where they live (computer/other-ai-files.mjs, tool:other-ai-files). Nothing is copied into Trillion or written back to those folders. `sources` is one row per AI app; each `places` row says what kind of thing it holds and its shape: `file` (one file), `files` (every file in a folder with the given endings) or `skill_folders` (each folder inside it that holds `file`) or `mcp_servers` (the servers one JSON file lists under `key`: each is listed and read as its command or address with the NAMES of its environment variables, never their values, and is only ever a description: nothing here switches a server on). A new AI app, or another folder, is one more row. Every path is read under the person's home folder, and a folder's symbolic links are never followed.",
  "most_files": 300,
  "most_chars": 20000,
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "claude-code",
      "label": "Claude Code",
      "places": [
        {
          "kind": "instructions",
          "shape": "file",
          "path": "~/.claude/CLAUDE.md"
        },
        {
          "kind": "commands",
          "shape": "files",
          "path": "~/.claude/commands",
          "endings": [
            ".md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "skills",
          "shape": "skill_folders",
          "path": "~/.claude/skills",
          "file": "SKILL.md"
        },
        {
          "kind": "mcp_servers",
          "shape": "mcp_servers",
          "path": "~/.claude.json",
          "key": "mcpServers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
